Build an industry-grade adaptive Hard Rules Engine as a stateless and concurrent Rust microservice.

==================================================
OBJECTIVE
==================================================

The service acts as a deterministic security enforcement engine.

It receives incoming API requests from the main gateway, validates them against predefined hard security rules, and returns PASS or FAIL responses.

The engine must:
- process requests concurrently
- remain stateless
- scale horizontally
- support millions of requests
- use indexed in-memory rule matching
- support adaptive AI-assisted rule learning
- dynamically reload rules without restarting

This service does NOT handle:
- authentication
- JWT validation
- API key validation
- rate limiting
- load balancing
- semantic reasoning
- orchestration

Those are handled by the main gateway.

==================================================
CORE ARCHITECTURE
==================================================

Main Gateway
      ↓
Rust Hard Rules Engine
      ↓
Indexed Rule Matching Engine
      ↓
PASS / FAIL Response

==================================================
ADAPTIVE RULE LEARNING FLOW
==================================================

Request
   ↓
Indexed Rule Matching

IF Rule Exists:
   Return PASS / FAIL immediately

IF No Rule Matches:
   Forward request to AI agent
      ↓
   AI analyzes unknown pattern
      ↓
   Generate suggested rule/signature
      ↓
   Validate generated rule
      ↓
   Store approved rule in PostgreSQL
      ↓
   Dynamically reload runtime indexes
      ↓
   Return final PASS / FAIL response

