==================================================
SUPPORTED HARD RULE TYPES
==================================================

1. SQL Injection Detection
- DROP TABLE
- UNION SELECT
- OR 1=1
- xp_cmdshell

2. Dangerous Command Detection
- rm -rf
- chmod 777
- curl | sh
- powershell execution

3. Restricted Operations
- filesystem deletion
- credential exposure
- shell execution attempts

4. Founder/Manager Custom Rules
- blocked keywords
- protected APIs
- restricted resources

5. Request Validation
- malformed JSON
- oversized payloads
- invalid schema

==================================================
RULE STORAGE ARCHITECTURE
==================================================

PostgreSQL acts as:
- persistent rule store
- rule versioning system
- searchable rule database
- adaptive rule storage

The runtime engine must:
- load rules at startup
- compile regex at startup
- build in-memory indexes
- dynamically reload indexes when rules update

==================================================
RULE MATCHING ARCHITECTURE
==================================================

Use multi-layer indexed matching:

Layer 1:
- tokenization

Layer 2:
- Aho-Corasick multi-pattern matching

Layer 3:
- candidate rule filtering

Layer 4:
- precompiled regex verification

Layer 5:
- final PASS / FAIL decision

